 "section_summary": "This section comprises pages 353 to 413 of a comprehensive official register (document series AR-231-CR-E-1) listing Japanese designated Historic Sites (H.S.), Places of Scenic Beauty (S.S.), and Natural Monuments (N.H.P.). Arranged by prefecture—spanning Fukui, Yamanashi, Nagano, Gifu, Shiga, Shizuoka, Aichi, Mie, Kyoto, Osaka, Hyogo, Nara, Wakayama, Tottori, Shimane, Okayama, Hiroshima, Yamaguchi, Tokushima, Kagawa, Ehime, Kochi, and Fukuoka—the catalogue records each property's name, preservation classification, legal rationale, designation date from 1920 to 1944, managing administrator, and local administrative jurisdiction. The protected sites include ancient burial mounds (kofun), Buddhist temple ruins, castle fortifications, Emperor Meiji's sojourn and resting places (anzaisho and goshokeijo), primeval forests, rare botanical and zoological habitats, and prominent geological formations.",
