   "start_page": 353,
   "summary": "This section of the register catalogs hundreds of nationally protected cultural, historical, and natural properties across twenty-three prefectures from Fukui to Fukuoka. Each entry specifies the site name, preservation classification (Historic Site, Scenic Beauty, or Natural Monument), reason and date of designation between 1920 and 1944, managing administrator, and local administrative jurisdiction. The listings encompass ancient tumuli, Buddhist temples, feudal castle ruins, Emperor Meiji memorial sites, primeval forests, botanical and zoological habitats, and prominent geological landmarks.",
   "title": "Catalogue of Designated Historic Sites, Places of Scenic Beauty, and Natural Monuments in Japan (AR-231-CR-E-1)",
